	"notes": "Cell px: pixel (x, y) covers [x, x + 1] x [y, y + 1]. The cell's origin is drawn at the player Visual's origin (the cell centre: the Visual's offset is -origin), scale game px per cell px (the Visual's scale); a left strike mirrors the side row about the origin. A frame's Sprite2D frame is row * 8 + column, its column the frame number - 1. socket: the neck's end on frames with the spear out (part / full), where the rigid spear's visible part starts, the spear along aim through it; on hidden frames the body's front edge on the line of frame 4's socket (nothing is drawn). bump: the painted bump's tip, where the baked neck leaves the body (the spear's hidden end can start behind it, inside the jelly). neck_fade_end: where the baked neck has faded into the shaft. socket_game: the socket in game px from the Visual's origin. shaft_px: the game-px shaft width the neck's end was baked to. source_scale: cell px per source px of the strip; rest_centre / ground / anchor: where the rest frame stands (page 1's idle frame's middle and ground: the bottom edge of the solid px on the side, the feet's in the front and back views), and the strip's fixed back (side) or middle (down / up) on the ground. rest_frame: the frame (1-6) to hold at rest (frame 1 of the jab is drawn about 7 percent taller and would pop).",
