		"notes": "The War Axe's and the Hammer's strike frames (scripts/characters/pack-slime-weapon-strikes.py; docs/design/2026-10-12-weapon-strike-frames.md). Per strike: its sheet (`texture`), its weapon block (`weapon`), per direction the sheet row (a `flip` strip shows its `source` strike's row mirrored; its frames and keys are the source row's, unmirrored), per frame the socket (the knob's tip, cell px; `socket_game`: game px from the Visual's origin, the slime's centre) and `knob_w` (the knob's chord, game px: the code neck's root width), and the timeline `keys`: `at` w|a|r<share> of the step's windupMs / activeMs / recoveryMs; each key's frame shows from its `at`, its angle / length / head_angle are eased linearly (as numbers) to the next key's; a value a key leaves out is the previous key's, head_angle the key's own angle; layer steps. Angles: screen degrees in the strip's own frame (0 right, +90 down), from the socket along the handle. The game (shape_visuals.gd _strike_weapon_at) draws the weapon rigid at `scale`: the neck (neck.webp, root_x on the socket, uniformly scaled by knob_w / width_px) ends neck_len = (tip_x - root_x) x that scale from the socket; the strip's jelly arm (`arm_px`, per direction) stretches the neck's cone (root_x to tip_x) by arm_px, so the neck's tip is neck_len + arm_px out; the handle (texture x 0 to head_start, row axis_row on the axis, handle_across x scale thick) stretched from hidden_px behind the socket to handle_px past the neck's tip (the joint), the head from the joint at head_angle; the whole slid back along the axis by (1 - length) x (hidden_px + joint + the head's depth) and cut at the hidden end; `front` draws the part past the neck's tip over the world, as does a `behind` weapon pointing down (axis y > 0.5) on a downward aim. Mirrored: x negated, a -> 180 - a, the textures reflected across the axis. head_centre, face_row, socket_to_head_px, handle_width_game, head_depth_game, head_height_game: for reference. `contact` (p